From 0bbc113bf3251b70ac1ad34f3964996a0b11a8a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 04:08:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] phy: add Realtek RTL819x USB2 PHY

Add a driver for the two UTMI PHYs of the Realtek RTL819x MIPS SoCs.
The PHYs are taken out of reset and powered on through the system
controller; electrical tuning parameters are applied through the
indirect UTMI access (data written to the analog block, address
strobed by a Synopsys vendor register in the EHCI MMIO space),
selected by the 25/40 MHz crystal strap.

port_init() takes the PHY out of reset before it configures it, so
every phy_init() - the configuration entry point - starts from a reset
PHY rather than from whatever the boot code or a previous host left;
the same line is pulsed again once the parameters are written, which is
what latches them.

For now both PHYs are wired to the host controllers in dual-host
mode; OTG device support through the DWC controller will need mode
negotiation on the shared PHY.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
